ue of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 45 of them. In 2025, March to April ran 190% of normal on the middle of the grids, then November to December fell to 34%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 14% and March to April at 18%. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, with grid 17215 down to 34% of normal that year.</p>"}
